---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import StepsStrip from '../components/StepsStrip.astro';

const faq = [
  {
    q: 'Will rotating cost me quality?',
    a: 'No. The words and pictures on the pages are not redrawn or re-encoded; only the turn setting each page carries is changed, so the finished file is as sharp as the one you brought, and almost the same size.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Only one page is sideways. Must I turn them all?',
    a: 'No. Pick "one page range" and give that page twice (from 3, to 3, for the third page). Just that page turns.',
  },
  {
    q: 'A page was already turned. What happens?',
    a: 'Turns add up. A page already carrying a quarter turn to the right, given another quarter turn to the right here, ends up carrying a half turn. If a page ends up wrong, bring the finished file back and turn it again until it sits right; nothing is lost by turning.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Where does my document go?',
    a: 'Nowhere. It is read into this page and rotated in your browser. Watch the network panel while it works if you want to check.',
  },
];
const faqJson = JSON.stringify({
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faq.map((f) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: f.q, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a } })),
});
const howToJson = JSON.stringify({
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'HowTo',
  name: "How to rotate a PDF",
  step: [
    { '@type': 'HowToStep', position: 1, name: "Pick the PDF", text: "Drop a PDF on the tray, or click to pick one. It stays on this device. The page reads its page count before anything runs." },
    { '@type': 'HowToStep', position: 2, name: "Choose the turn", text: "Pick a quarter turn to the right, a half turn, or a quarter turn to the left, and whether it applies to every page or one page range." },
    { '@type': 'HowToStep', position: 3, name: "Rotate the PDF", text: "Press 'Rotate the PDF'. The turn setting on each chosen page is changed and the file is saved; the pages themselves are not redrawn." },
    { '@type': 'HowToStep', position: 4, name: "Download the rotated PDF", text: "Take the finished file away. The result line reports the turns the finished file actually carries." },
  ],
});
---

<Base title="Rotate PDF: turn pages 90, 180 or 270 degrees, free · Benchzy" description="Rotate every page of a PDF, or one page range, by a quarter or half turn, inside your browser. The turn is a setting the file carries; nothing is redrawn and nothing is uploaded.">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4">
    <section class="mt-8">
      <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-accent-deep">PDF tools · pages</p>
      <h1 class="font-display text-4xl font-black mt-2">Rotate PDF</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-lg leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
        Turn the pages of a PDF the right way up and save them that way: every page, or one
        page range, by a quarter turn or a half turn. Everything runs in your browser; the
        document is never uploaded.
      </p>
    </section>

    <StepsStrip who="For a scan that came out sideways, a sideways sheet saved into a PDF, or a file a portal keeps showing you lying on its side." steps={[{ n: '01', t: 'Pick the PDF' }, { n: '02', t: 'Choose the turn' }, { n: '03', t: 'Rotate and download' }]} />

    <section class="ticket mt-6 p-5 sm:p-7" id="rt-tool">
      <div id="rt-tray" class="tray p-6 text-center cursor-pointer" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Pick a PDF">
        <p class="font-display text-xl font-bold">Drop a PDF on the tray, or click to pick one</p>
        <p class="font-mono text-xs text-ink-soft mt-2">PDF · it stays on this device</p>
        <input id="rt-file" type="file" accept="application/pdf,.pdf" class="hidden" />
      </div>
      <p class="file-loaded hidden" data-loaded-for="rt-file" role="status"></p>

      <div class="grid gap-6 mt-6 md:grid-cols-[1fr_320px]">
        <div>
          <h2 class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-soft">The turn</h2>
          <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3">
            <label class="flex items-baseline gap-2">
              <input type="radio" name="rt-angle" value="90" checked />
              <span>A quarter turn to the right (90°)</span>
            </label>
            <label class="flex items-baseline gap-2">
              <input type="radio" name="rt-angle" value="180" />
              <span>A half turn (180°)</span>
            </label>
            <label class="flex items-baseline gap-2">
              <input type="radio" name="rt-angle" value="270" />
              <span>A quarter turn to the left (270°)</span>
            </label>
          </div>
          <h2 class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-soft mt-6">Which pages</h2>
          <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3">
            <label class="flex items-baseline gap-2">
              <input type="radio" name="rt-scope" value="all" checked />
              <span>Every page</span>
            </label>
            <label class="flex items-baseline gap-2">
              <input type="radio" name="rt-scope" value="range" />
              <span>One page range</span>
            </label>
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 ml-6 flex-wrap">
              <label class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-soft" for="rt-from">From page</label>
              <input id="rt-from" type="number" min="1" step="1" value="1" class="border border-ink bg-ticket px-3 py-2 font-mono w-24" />
              <label class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-soft" for="rt-to">To page</label>
              <input id="rt-to" type="number" min="1" step="1" value="1" class="border border-ink bg-ticket px-3 py-2 font-mono w-24" />
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2 class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-soft">File spec</h2>
          <dl id="rt-spec" class="mt-2">
            <div class="spec-row"><dt>file</dt><dd>none picked yet</dd></div>
          </dl>
          <p class="action-note">
            The turn is a setting the file carries, like turning a printed sheet in the tray:
            the words and pictures are not redrawn, so nothing can lose quality.
          </p>
          <button id="rt-run" class="btn-primary w-full mt-5" type="button" disabled>Rotate the PDF</button>
          <p id="rt-status" class="font-mono text-sm mt-4 leading-relaxed" aria-live="polite">Pick a PDF to begin.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div id="rt-result" class="receipt hidden mt-8">
        <div class="tear pt-5 flex items-center gap-4 flex-wrap">
          <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold">Result</h2>
          <span class="stamp" id="rt-stamp">Done on your device</span>
        </div>
        <p id="rt-achieved" class="mt-3 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl"></p>
        <a id="rt-download" class="btn-primary inline-block no-underline mt-3" href="#" download>Download the rotated PDF</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-12 grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold border-b-2 border-ink pb-2">How it works</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          Rotation is a setting each page carries inside the file, and readers turn the page
          because the file says so. This page changes that setting on the pages you picked
          and saves the file. The download is how we protect your privacy: the program that
          does this job is part of this page, loaded from this site, and your file is read
          into the page and never uploaded. The finished file is opened again and its turns
          counted, so the result line reports the file's own numbers, not the plan.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold border-b-2 border-ink pb-2">Honest limits</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          The turn applies to whole pages. It cannot straighten a photo that sits crooked
          inside its page, because that crookedness is part of the page's picture, not a
          page setting; that is an editing job, not a page turn. Turns add to any turn a
          page already carries.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">A password-protected PDF cannot be opened by this tool. Take its password off first with the <a class="underline underline-offset-4" href="/unlock-pdf/">unlock tool</a>, then bring the file back.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 mb-4">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold border-b-2 border-ink pb-2">Questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-4 grid gap-4">
        {faq.map((f) => (
          <article class="ticket-soft p-5">
            <h3 class="font-bold">{f.q}</h3>
            <p class="text-ink-soft leading-relaxed mt-1">{f.a}</p>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={faqJson}></script>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={howToJson}></script>
  <script>
    import '../scripts/rotate-pdf.js';
  </script>
</Base>
